{"name":"Pier Feather","hex":"#d9d9d2","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pier","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A raised platform built from the shore out over water, supported on piles; used to secure, or provide access to shipping; a jetty.","A similar structure, especially at a seaside resort, used to provide entertainment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pier"},{"term":"feather","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A branching, hair-like structure that grows on the bodies of birds, used for flight, swimming, protection and display.","Long hair on the lower legs of a dog or horse, especially a draft horse, notably the Clydesdale breed. Narrowly only the rear hair."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover or furnish with feathers;  to fletch.","To adorn, as if with feathers; to fringe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feather"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pier","blocks":[{"text":"A pier is a raised structure that rises above a body of water and usually juts out from its shore, typically supported by piles or pillars, and provides above-water access to offshore areas. Frequent pier uses include fishing, boat docking and access for both passengers and cargo, and oceanside recreation such as swimming. Bridges, buildings, and walkways may all be supported by architectural piers. Their open structure allows tides and currents to flow relatively unhindered, whereas the more solid foundations of a quay or the closely spaced piles of a wharf can act as a breakwater, and are consequently more liable to silting. Piers can range in size and complexity from a simple lightweight wooden structure to major structures extended over 1,600 m (5,200 ft). In American English, a pier may be synonymous with a dock."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Korfu_%28GR%29%2C_Korfu%2C_Altstadt_--_2018_--_1156.jpg/330px-Korfu_%28GR%29%2C_Korfu%2C_Altstadt_--_2018_--_1156.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pier","wikidata":"Q863454"},{"title":"Feather","blocks":[{"text":"Feathers are epidermal growths that form a distinctive outer covering, or plumage, on both avian (bird) and some non-avian dinosaurs and other archosaurs. They are the most complex integumentary structures found in vertebrates and an example of a complex evolutionary novelty. They are among the characteristics that distinguish the extant birds from other living groups."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Types_de_plumes._-_Larousse_pour_tous%2C_-1907-1910-.jpg/330px-Types_de_plumes._-_Larousse_pour_tous%2C_-1907-1910-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feather","wikidata":"Q81025"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Korfu_%28GR%29%2C_Korfu%2C_Altstadt_--_2018_--_1156.jpg/500px-Korfu_%28GR%29%2C_Korfu%2C_Altstadt_--_2018_--_1156.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Korfu_%28GR%29%2C_Korfu%2C_Altstadt_--_2018_--_1156.jpg/1280px-Korfu_%28GR%29%2C_Korfu%2C_Altstadt_--_2018_--_1156.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Korfu_%28GR%29%2C_Korfu%2C_Altstadt_--_2018_--_1156.jpg/500px-Korfu_%28GR%29%2C_Korfu%2C_Altstadt_--_2018_--_1156.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A wooden pier in Corfu, Greece","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKorfu_(GR)%2C_Korfu%2C_Altstadt_--_2018_--_1156.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Under_the_pier%2C_Nikiski.jpg/500px-Under_the_pier%2C_Nikiski.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Under_the_pier%2C_Nikiski.jpg/1280px-Under_the_pier%2C_Nikiski.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Under_the_pier%2C_Nikiski.jpg/500px-Under_the_pier%2C_Nikiski.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Out-of-use industrial bulk cargo Pier, Cook Inlet, Alaska.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUnder_the_pier%2C_Nikiski.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/The_jetty%2C_Margate%2C_Kent%2C_England%2C_ca._1897.jpg/500px-The_jetty%2C_Margate%2C_Kent%2C_England%2C_ca._1897.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/The_jetty%2C_Margate%2C_Kent%2C_England%2C_ca._1897.jpg/1280px-The_jetty%2C_Margate%2C_Kent%2C_England%2C_ca._1897.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/The_jetty%2C_Margate%2C_Kent%2C_England%2C_ca._1897.jpg/500px-The_jetty%2C_Margate%2C_Kent%2C_England%2C_ca._1897.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Print of a Victorian pier in Margate in the English county of Kent, 1897","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_jetty%2C_Margate%2C_Kent%2C_England%2C_ca._1897.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Pretty_when_it_sleeps.jpg/500px-Pretty_when_it_sleeps.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Pretty_when_it_sleeps.jpg/1280px-Pretty_when_it_sleeps.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Pretty_when_it_sleeps.jpg/500px-Pretty_when_it_sleeps.jpg?utm_source=en.wikip